---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="UK Visa to ILR Roadmap – Steps to Settlement | AfriMigrate"
  description="Free step-by-step roadmap from a UK Skilled Worker visa to Indefinite Leave to Remain (ILR) and British citizenship."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/uk">UK</a> / Visa to ILR Roadmap</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">UK · Settlement</div>
  <h1>Visa to ILR Roadmap</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    Indefinite Leave to Remain (ILR) removes all restrictions on how long you can stay in the UK. Most Skilled Worker visa holders reach it after five continuous years — here's the realistic path.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">The Journey</div>
    <h2>Five years, four milestones</h2>
    <div class="steps" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);">
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">1</div><h3>Year 0</h3><p>Enter the UK on your first Skilled Worker visa, typically granted for up to 5 years.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">2</div><h3>Years 1–4</h3><p>Stay continuously sponsored. Absences of more than 180 days in any 12-month rolling period can reset your clock.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">3</div><h3>Year 5</h3><p>Apply for ILR: pass the Life in the UK test and prove English at B1, meet the salary/continuous employment requirement.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">4</div><h3>Year 6+</h3><p>After 12 months holding ILR, most people become eligible to apply for British citizenship.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Watch Out For</div>
    <h2>The most common ways people delay themselves</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Risk</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Long absences from the UK</td><td>More than 180 days out in any rolling 12 months can break "continuous residence"</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Changing sponsor without updating your visa</td><td>Working for an unsponsored employer, even briefly, can breach your visa conditions</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Salary dropping below threshold</td><td>ILR requires you to still meet the going rate for your role at the time of application</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Letting your visa lapse before renewing</td><td>Any gap in valid leave can restart your continuous residence clock</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Before You Land</div>
    <h2>Get the costs sorted first</h2>
    <p class="lead">Budget for your full five-year journey, not just the first visa — renewals and the IHS add up.</p>
    <a href="/uk/visa-cost-calculator" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Calculate visa costs →</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
